RandomSeed [SimTalk] - Method/User-defined Attribute
Sets the random number stream of the Method designated by the reference operator <&> or of the
user-defined attribute of data type Method or RandTime.
Remarks
As you are used to from the material flow objects, Plant Simulation automatically assigns the random
number seed value when you insert an object, so that each object has its own random number seed value.
If you call one of the distribution functions in a Method, the first parameter, which specifies the random
number stream, is optional. If you do not specify the stream, Plant Simulation uses the random number
stream of the Method or of the user-defined attribute of data type method.
This affects the following distribution functions:
z_beta, z_binomial, z_cEmp, dEmp, z_emp, z_erlang, z_frechet, z_gamma, z_geom, z_gumbel,
z_hypgeom, z_laplace, z_logistic, z_logLogistic z_lognorm, z_negexp, z_normal, z_paraLogistic, z_pareto,
z_poisson, z_triangle, z_uniform, and z_weibull.
You can still call the distribution functions with the parameter for the random number stream as you did
in previous versions. For formulas it is required, as formulas never use the random number stream of the
surrounding object.
The random number sequences, which are generated by the random number streams of the Methods,
differ from the random number sequences of the global random number streams, whose seed values you
can set under File > Options > Random Number Seed Values even if they have the same random number
seed value.
Plant Simulation keeps a common seed value in the object. Plant Simulation automatically assigns the
random number value when inserting an object, but only if the object can create random numbers. This is
then the case when the object itself can create random numbers, for example a Station for its Processing
Time, or when the object has a user-defined attribute of data type Method or RandTime. If both is not the
case, Plant Simulation assigns the value 0 to the attribute RandomSeed when inserting the object. If the
value of the attribute RandomSeed is 0, the attribute will not be shown in the window Show Attributes
and Methods and will not be written to the folder model. When you create a user-defined attribute of data
type Method or RandTime for such an object, Plant Simulation sets a random number value automatically
as well.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<&>Method.RandomSeed:integer
RandomSeed [SimTalk] - Method/User-defined Attribute
Plant Simulation Help 11-3721
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Examples
&Method1.RandomSeed := 1313
DataTable.RandomSeed := 101
