UsingNewSyntax [SimTalk]
Activates (true) SimTalk 2.0 syntax for the Method designated by the reference operator <&> or
deactivates it (false).
Remarks
Note
Clicking 
  for an existing Method, whose source code you created in SimTalk 1.0 notation,
automatically converts that source code to source code in the correct SimTalk 2.0 notation.
If UsingNewSyntax is active, you have to enter the source code into Methods in the improved, abbreviated
SimTalk 2.0 notation.
If you want to use SimTalk 2.0 syntax for all new Methods which you are going to program, activate
UsingNewSyntax in the Method class in the Class Library.
Plant Simulation writes the setting UsingNewSyntax to the model file.
If UsingNewSyntax is deactivated, you have to enter the source code into Methods using SimTalk 1.0
notation.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<&>Method.UsingNewSyntax:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
&Method1.UsingNewSyntax := true
UsingNewSyntax [SimTalk]
